  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Watershed Investment Program: Workplan and Partnership arrangement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Watershed investment programs (WIPs), including Waterfunds, conservation trust funds (CTFs) have been successful in mitigating and overcoming Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) challenges. Promoters, like the World Wildlife Fund (WWF), CI, IUCN and World Resource Institute (WRI), need assistance to set up and operationalise these WIPs effectively and sustainable. Structuring and managing WIPs - and developing them at scale - requires dedicated support. To advance in the setup of a Watershed Developer Investment (WADI) Platform and pilot these within the ongoing collaboration between TNC, WaterWorX, Blue Deal on the ground, the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) aims to step in as a partner to implement and co-finance this process. In order to secure this partnership in a partnership agreement, a detailed workplan is required. This assignment is aimed to establish a detailed workplan that outlines:&#x2022;	The activities of the partnership in developing WADI and piloting WIPs for a duration of one year;&#x2022;	Clear deliverables of the (in-kind) partnership activities and interconnectedness;&#x2022;	Roles and responsibilities of each partner to achieve the deliverables;&#x2022;	Governance of the partnership (suggested collaboration arrangement);&#x2022;	Detailed planning with (intermittent) milestones; and&#x2022;	Detailed activity budget.</narrative>
  </description>
